IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ohsr-dates`
IMPORT `ohsr-core`

-- Occupational Health and Safety Regulations 2017 (Vic) -- from the seat of the worker.
--
-- SEAT: the individual the Regulations protect at work: an employee (and, where r 8 or the regulation extends the duty,
-- an independent contractor or a contractor's employee), including one who has been injured, has fallen ill or fears an
-- illness from the work, and a person applying for such work. "Did my employer have to do this? Has it breached the
-- regulation? Is my exposure over the limit? When is my next test due? Must I be taken off the work, and when may I go
-- back? Can I see the records, and how long must they be kept? Was WorkSafe told in time? What is the most the employer
-- can be fined?" Every question is asked as that person would ask it, on facts they can state; the court's,
-- the doctor's and WorkSafe's judgments are facts the person answers from what they have been told. The rules are in
-- ohsr-core.l4; this module builds their inputs from plain answers and restates no rule. Inputs with the same meaning
-- have the same name in every question, so the form can ask them once.
--
-- MAYBE BOOLEAN answers: JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE the text says no on these facts; NOTHING the text does not settle it.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Occupational Health and Safety Regulations 2017 -- the questions of the worker`

§§ `Whether the Regulations' duties reach me (r 8)`

@export Do the employer duties in Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Regulations 2017 reach me, as an employee or as an independent contractor (or a contractor's employee) the business engaged?
GIVEN `I am the business's employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed by the business (under a contract of employment or training)
      `I am an independent contractor the business engaged, or a contractor's employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business engaged you as an independent contractor, or you work for an independent contractor it engaged
      `the matter is within the business's control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk concerns a matter the business controls, or would control but for an agreement limiting its control
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the Regulations' employer duties reach me` IS
    `the employer's duty reaches the person (r 8)` `I am the business's employee` `I am an independent contractor the business engaged, or a contractor's employee` `the matter is within the business's control`

§§ `Health monitoring and medical examinations in general (rr 18-20)`

@export Must my employer pay for the medical examination or health monitoring the Regulations require for me (r 19(3))?
GIVEN `the Regulations require the examination or monitoring` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation requires your employer to have you medically examined or your health monitored (for example audiometric tests for noise, health monitoring for a Schedule 9 substance, blood lead tests, asbestos medicals)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer pay for my health monitoring` IS
    `the employer must pay for the examination or monitoring (r 19(3))` `the Regulations require the examination or monitoring`

@export Has my employer breached r 19 (it must tell me the purpose and nature of the medical examination or health monitoring the Regulations require, and must not charge me for it)?
GIVEN `the Regulations require the examination or monitoring` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation requires your employer to have you medically examined or your health monitored (for example audiometric tests for noise, health monitoring for a Schedule 9 substance, blood lead tests, asbestos medicals)
      `my employer told me its purpose and nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer told you what the examination or monitoring is for and what kind it is
      `I was charged for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were made to pay any of its cost
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer breached r 19` IS
    `r 19 was contravened` `the Regulations require the examination or monitoring` `my employer told me its purpose and nature` `I was charged for it`

@export May my employer give my medical examination or health monitoring report (or its summary) to this person, under r 20 of Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Regulations 2017?
GIVEN `who would receive it` IS A `Report recipient` @desc Who would receive it: you yourself; a third party you have authorised in writing; WorkSafe, on request or where the Regulations require; or anyone else
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my employer give my health report to this person` IS
    `the report may be disclosed to the recipient (r 20)` `who would receive it`

@export Has a control measure the Regulations required been left improperly installed, used or maintained (r 18)?
GIVEN `the measure is required by the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation required this particular measure to control the risk (for example guarding, local exhaust ventilation, a fall arrest system)
      `the measure is one Part 5.2 or 5.3 requires (major hazard facilities or mines)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the measure is one required by the Regulations' Parts on major hazard facilities or mines
      `the measure was properly installed, used and maintained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the measure was properly installed (where that applies), used and maintained
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was a required control measure not properly kept up` IS
    `r 18 was contravened` `the measure is required by the Regulations` `the measure is one Part 5.2 or 5.3 requires (major hazard facilities or mines)` `the measure was properly installed, used and maintained`

§§ `Controlling a hazard and reviewing the controls (rr 27, 34, 44, 56, 98, 163, 184, 238, 325 and the review regulations)`

@export Did my employer break the order of control the Regulations set for this hazard (eliminate the risk first; then the measures the Part names, in order; information, administrative controls or protective equipment last)?
GIVEN `the hazard` IS A `Hazard` @desc The hazard: hazardous manual handling; noise; a fall of more than 2 metres; work in a confined space; plant; a hazardous substance; lead; asbestos at the workplace; or construction work
      `the main measure used` IS A `Control measure` @desc The highest-order measure your employer relied on (eliminating the risk; altering layout, environment or systems; changing the things handled; mechanical aids; substitution; isolation; engineering controls; a passive fall prevention device; a work positioning system; a fall arrest system; a ladder; administrative controls; information, instruction or training; personal protective equipment including hearing protectors; enclosing or sealing asbestos; other measures; or none)
      `the best measure that was reasonably practicable` IS A `Control measure` @desc The highest-order measure that was reasonably practicable for this hazard (a question for the court, from the same list)
      `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, with the measures used, the risk was reduced so far as was reasonably practicable (a question for the court)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did my employer break the order of control` IS
    `the control duty was contravened` `the hazard` `the main measure used` `the best measure that was reasonably practicable` `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable`

@export Must my employer now review, and if necessary revise, its controls for this hazard?
GIVEN `the hazard` IS A `Hazard` @desc The hazard: hazardous manual handling; noise; a fall of more than 2 metres; work in a confined space; plant; a hazardous substance; lead; asbestos at the workplace; or construction work
      `what has happened` IS A `Review occasion` @desc What has happened: a change to the work, plant or system of work is about to be made; new information about the hazard; a musculoskeletal disorder was reported; an audiological report found noise-induced hearing loss; health monitoring found adverse effects; a worker was removed from lead-risk work; an incident under Part 5 of the Act; the controls do not adequately control the risk; the health and safety representative asked; or none of these
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer review its controls` IS
    `the controls must be reviewed` `the hazard` `what has happened`

§§ `Hazardous manual handling (Part 3.1)`

@export Is my work "hazardous manual handling" under r 5 of Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Regulations 2017?
GIVEN `the work needs me to use force to lift, lower, push, pull, carry, move, hold or restrain something` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work needs you to use force to lift, lower, push, pull, carry or otherwise move, hold or restrain something or someone
      `it involves repetitive or sustained force, awkward posture, repetitive movement, high force or sustained vibration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involves repetitive or sustained force, sustained awkward posture, repetitive movement, high force a person might reasonably find difficult, or sustained vibration
      `I handle live people or animals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you handle is a live person or animal
      `the load is unstable, unbalanced or hard to grasp` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the load is unstable, unbalanced or difficult to grasp or hold
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work hazardous manual handling` IF
    `the work is hazardous manual handling (r 5)` `the work needs me to use force to lift, lower, push, pull, carry, move, hold or restrain something` `it involves repetitive or sustained force, awkward posture, repetitive movement, high force or sustained vibration` `I handle live people or animals` `the load is unstable, unbalanced or hard to grasp`

@export Is my injury a "musculoskeletal disorder" under r 5 (an injury, illness or disease arising in whole or part from hazardous manual handling)?
GIVEN `my injury arose in whole or in part from hazardous manual handling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury, illness or disease arose wholly or partly from hazardous manual handling, suddenly or over time
      `my injury was crushing, entrapment or cutting caused mainly by a machine's operation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was crushing, entrapment or cutting caused mainly by the mechanical operation of plant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my injury a musculoskeletal disorder` IF
    `the injury is a musculoskeletal disorder (r 5)` `my injury arose in whole or in part from hazardous manual handling` `my injury was crushing, entrapment or cutting caused mainly by a machine's operation`

@export Has my employer breached its hazardous manual handling duties (r 26 identify the hazard; r 27 eliminate the risk, or reduce it by changing the layout, environment, systems or things handled or by mechanical aids, with training only as a last resort)?
GIVEN `the work needs me to use force to lift, lower, push, pull, carry, move, hold or restrain something` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work needs you to use force to lift, lower, push, pull, carry or otherwise move, hold or restrain something or someone
      `it involves repetitive or sustained force, awkward posture, repetitive movement, high force or sustained vibration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involves repetitive or sustained force, sustained awkward posture, repetitive movement, high force a person might reasonably find difficult, or sustained vibration
      `I handle live people or animals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you handle is a live person or animal
      `the load is unstable, unbalanced or hard to grasp` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the load is unstable, unbalanced or difficult to grasp or hold
      `my employer identified the hazardous manual handling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer identified the hazardous manual handling so far as reasonably practicable
      `the main measure used` IS A `Control measure` @desc The highest-order measure your employer relied on: eliminating the risk; altering the layout, environment or system of work; changing the things handled; mechanical aids; information, instruction or training; or none
      `the best measure that was reasonably practicable` IS A `Control measure` @desc The highest-order measure that was reasonably practicable (a question for the court, from the same list)
      `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, with the measures used, the risk was reduced so far as was reasonably practicable (a question for the court)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer breached the manual handling duties` IS
    `Part 3.1 was contravened (rr 26, 27)`
        (`the work is hazardous manual handling (r 5)` `the work needs me to use force to lift, lower, push, pull, carry, move, hold or restrain something` `it involves repetitive or sustained force, awkward posture, repetitive movement, high force or sustained vibration` `I handle live people or animals` `the load is unstable, unbalanced or hard to grasp`)
        `my employer identified the hazardous manual handling`
        `the main measure used`
        `the best measure that was reasonably practicable`
        `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable`

§§ `Noise and hearing (Part 3.2)`

@export Is my noise exposure above Victoria's noise exposure standard (85 dB(A) averaged over 8 hours, or a 140 dB(C) peak, at my ear, ignoring hearing protectors)?
GIVEN `my 8-hour average noise level in dB(A)` IS A NUMBER @desc Your 8-hour equivalent continuous noise level, in A-weighted decibels, at your ear position without hearing protectors
      `my peak noise level in dB(C)` IS A NUMBER @desc The highest C-weighted peak noise level you are exposed to, in decibels, at your ear position
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my noise exposure above the standard` IF
    `the noise exposure standard is exceeded (r 5)` `my 8-hour average noise level in dB(A)` `my peak noise level in dB(C)`

@export Must my employer measure (determine) my noise exposure (r 32)?
GIVEN `there are reasonable grounds to be unsure whether the standard is or may be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there are reasonable grounds for uncertainty about whether your exposure is or may be above the noise exposure standard
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer measure my noise exposure` IS
    `the employer must determine the exposure (r 32)` `there are reasonable grounds to be unsure whether the standard is or may be exceeded`

@export Has my employer breached r 34 (no employee exposed above the noise exposure standard; quieter plant and engineering controls before administrative controls, hearing protectors last)?
GIVEN `the noise I still receive, with any hearing protectors, is above the standard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the noise reaching you, with any hearing protectors you were given, is still above the noise exposure standard
      `the main measure used` IS A `Control measure` @desc The highest-order measure your employer relied on: eliminating the noise source; substitution of quieter plant or processes; engineering controls; administrative controls; hearing protectors (personal protective equipment); or none
      `the best measure that was reasonably practicable` IS A `Control measure` @desc The highest-order measure that was reasonably practicable (a question for the court, from the same list)
      `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, with the measures used, your exposure was reduced so far as was reasonably practicable (a question for the court)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer breached the noise control duty` IS
    `r 34 was contravened` `the noise I still receive, with any hearing protectors, is above the standard` `the main measure used` `the best measure that was reasonably practicable` `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable`

@export Must my employer give me audiometric (hearing) tests under r 37?
GIVEN `I must be given hearing protectors under r 34(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer must provide you with hearing protectors because, after its other controls, your noise exposure is still above the standard
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be given audiometric tests` IS
    `audiometric testing is required (r 37)` `I must be given hearing protectors under r 34(5)`

@export By what day must my first audiometric test be done (within 3 months after I started the work needing hearing protectors, r 37(a))?
GIVEN `the day I started the work needing hearing protectors` IS A DATE @desc The day you started the work for which hearing protectors are required
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must my first audiometric test be done` IS
    `the last day for the first audiometric test (r 37(a))` `the day I started the work needing hearing protectors`

@export By what day is my next audiometric test due (at least every 2 years, r 37(c))?
GIVEN `the day of my last audiometric test` IS A DATE @desc The day of your most recent audiometric test
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when is my next audiometric test due` IS
    `the last day for the next audiometric test (r 37(c))` `the day of my last audiometric test`

@export Must my employer send me for an audiological examination (r 38: two audiometric tests no more than 2 years apart show my hearing fell by 15 dB or more at 3000, 4000 or 6000 Hz)?
GIVEN `the fall in my hearing at 3000 Hz in dB` IS A NUMBER @desc How many decibels your hearing level at 3000 Hz fell between the two tests
      `the fall in my hearing at 4000 Hz in dB` IS A NUMBER @desc How many decibels your hearing level at 4000 Hz fell between the two tests
      `the fall in my hearing at 6000 Hz in dB` IS A NUMBER @desc How many decibels your hearing level at 6000 Hz fell between the two tests
      `the day of the earlier test` IS A DATE @desc The day of the earlier of the two audiometric tests
      `the day of the later test` IS A DATE @desc The day of the later of the two audiometric tests
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be sent for an audiological examination` IS
    `an audiological examination is required (r 38)` `the fall in my hearing at 3000 Hz in dB` `the fall in my hearing at 4000 Hz in dB` `the fall in my hearing at 6000 Hz in dB` `the day of the earlier test` `the day of the later test`

@export Must my employer still keep my audiometric test results and audiological report (r 40(1))?
GIVEN `I still work for the employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are still employed by the employer
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer still keep my hearing test results` IS
    `the audiometric results must still be kept (r 40(1))` `I still work for the employer`

§§ `Falls (Part 3.3)`

@export Does Part 3.3 of Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Regulations 2017 (prevention of falls of more than 2 metres) apply to my task?
GIVEN `how far I could fall, in metres` IS A NUMBER @desc The height in metres you could fall while doing the task
      `the task is stunt work, acrobatics, a performance, sport, cycling or motorcycling, horse riding or rock climbing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the task is one of the activities r 41(2)(a) excludes: stunt work, acrobatics, a theatrical performance, a sporting activity, riding a bicycle, motorcycle or all-terrain vehicle, horse riding, rock climbing or recreational abseiling
      `the task is on compliant stairs, ladders, ramps or balconies used as designed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the task is on parts of a building (stairs, fixed ladders, ramps, balconies) that comply with AS 1657 and the Building Regulations and are used for their designed purpose
      `WorkSafe has excluded the activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe has determined that the activity is excluded from Part 3.3
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the falls Part apply to my task` IS
    `Part 3.3 applies to the task (r 41)` `how far I could fall, in metres` `the task is stunt work, acrobatics, a performance, sport, cycling or motorcycling, horse riding or rock climbing` `the task is on compliant stairs, ladders, ramps or balconies used as designed` `WorkSafe has excluded the activity`

@export Has my employer breached its duty to control my risk of a fall of more than 2 metres (r 44: eliminate it, else a passive fall prevention device, a work positioning system, a fall arrest system, then a ladder or administrative controls; r 45: a ladder fit for purpose and set up correctly)?
GIVEN `how far I could fall, in metres` IS A NUMBER @desc The height in metres you could fall while doing the task
      `the task is stunt work, acrobatics, a performance, sport, cycling or motorcycling, horse riding or rock climbing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the task is one of the activities r 41(2)(a) excludes: stunt work, acrobatics, a theatrical performance, a sporting activity, riding a bicycle, motorcycle or all-terrain vehicle, horse riding, rock climbing or recreational abseiling
      `the task is on compliant stairs, ladders, ramps or balconies used as designed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the task is on parts of a building (stairs, fixed ladders, ramps, balconies) that comply with AS 1657 and the Building Regulations and are used for their designed purpose
      `WorkSafe has excluded the activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe has determined that the activity is excluded from Part 3.3
      `the main measure used` IS A `Control measure` @desc The highest-order measure your employer relied on: eliminating the risk (for example working from the ground); a passive fall prevention device (guard rails, scaffolds, barriers); a work positioning system; a fall arrest system; a ladder; administrative controls; or none
      `the best measure that was reasonably practicable` IS A `Control measure` @desc The highest-order measure that was reasonably practicable (a question for the court, from the same list)
      `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, with the measures used, the risk was reduced so far as was reasonably practicable (a question for the court)
      `any ladder used was fit for purpose, suited to the task and set up correctly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a ladder was used, whether it was fit for the purpose, appropriate for how long the task took, and set up correctly (answer yes if no ladder was used)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer breached the fall control duty` IS
    `rr 44 and 45 were contravened`
        (`Part 3.3 applies to the task (r 41)` `how far I could fall, in metres` `the task is stunt work, acrobatics, a performance, sport, cycling or motorcycling, horse riding or rock climbing` `the task is on compliant stairs, ladders, ramps or balconies used as designed` `WorkSafe has excluded the activity`)
        `the main measure used`
        `the best measure that was reasonably practicable`
        `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable`
        `any ladder used was fit for purpose, suited to the task and set up correctly`

@export Must rescue and first aid procedures for a fall be in place before I start the task (r 49)?
GIVEN `the main measure used` IS A `Control measure` @desc The highest-order fall control your employer relies on: eliminating the risk; a passive fall prevention device; a work positioning system; a fall arrest system; a ladder; or administrative controls
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must fall rescue procedures be in place before I start` IS
    `fall emergency procedures are required before the task (r 49)` `the main measure used`

§§ `Confined spaces (Part 3.4) -- if your work takes you into a tank, pit, pipe, silo, sewer, trench or similar space`

@export Is the space I work in a "confined space" under r 5 of Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Regulations 2017?
GIVEN `it is a vat, tank, pit, pipe, duct, silo, sewer, well, shaft, trench, tunnel or similar enclosed structure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the space is in a vat, tank, pit, pipe, duct, flue, oven, chimney, silo, vessel, container, sewer, well, shaft, trench, tunnel or similar enclosed or partly enclosed structure
      `people enter or are likely to enter it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone enters, is meant to enter or is likely to enter the space
      `getting in or out is restricted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the way in or out is limited or restricted so that it is physically difficult to enter or leave
      `it is at normal air pressure while someone is in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the space is at normal atmospheric pressure while anyone is in it
      `it has or may have a harmful contaminant in the air` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the air in it contains, or may contain, a harmful level of a contaminant
      `it has or may have too little or too much oxygen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the air in it may not have a safe oxygen level (19.5% to 23.5%)
      `it holds or may hold a stored solid that could bury someone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it contains, or may contain, a stored substance (not a liquid) that could engulf a person
      `it is a shaft, trench or tunnel of a mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a shaft, trench or tunnel that is a mine or part of the workings of a mine
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a confined space` IF
    `the space is a confined space (r 5)` `it is a vat, tank, pit, pipe, duct, silo, sewer, well, shaft, trench, tunnel or similar enclosed structure` `people enter or are likely to enter it` `getting in or out is restricted` `it is at normal air pressure while someone is in it` `it has or may have a harmful contaminant in the air` `it has or may have too little or too much oxygen` `it holds or may hold a stored solid that could bury someone` `it is a shaft, trench or tunnel of a mine`

@export Is the oxygen level in the space safe under r 5 (19.5% to 23.5% by volume)?
GIVEN `the oxygen content in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc The oxygen content of the air in the space, in per cent by volume
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the oxygen level safe` IF
    `the atmosphere has a safe oxygen level (r 5)` `the oxygen content in per cent`

@export Must I be got out of the confined space immediately because of flammable gas (r 60: at 10% of the lower explosive limit or more; at 5% or more unless a continuous-monitoring gas detector is in use)?
GIVEN `the flammable gas level as a percentage of its lower explosive limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The concentration of flammable gas or vapour in the space, as a percentage of its lower explosive limit (LEL)
      `a calibrated continuous-monitoring gas detector is in use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a suitably calibrated, continuous-monitoring flammable gas detector is being used in the space while you are in it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be got out of the confined space now` IS
    `the employee must be removed from the space immediately (r 60)` `the flammable gas level as a percentage of its lower explosive limit` `a calibrated continuous-monitoring gas detector is in use`

@export Did my employer breach r 63 by letting me into a confined space without an entry permit for that space that named me?
GIVEN `I entered the confined space` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you entered the confined space
      `a permit for that space named me and was in operation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer had issued a confined space entry permit for that space, naming you, for a period that covered your entry
      `I am an emergency service worker rescuing or giving first aid on my employer's direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an emergency service employee who, at your employer's direction, was rescuing someone from the space or giving first aid in it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I let into the confined space without a permit` IS
    `r 63 was contravened` `I entered the confined space` `a permit for that space named me and was in operation` `I am an emergency service worker rescuing or giving first aid on my employer's direction`

@export Has my employer broken the working rules for my confined space work (safe air or air-supplied respirators, continuous communication, knowing who is inside, rehearsed rescue procedures, training)?
GIVEN `the air was safe or I had air-supplied respiratory equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the space had a safe oxygen level and no contaminant above its exposure standard, or you were given suitable (air-supplied where oxygen was unsafe) respiratory protective equipment (r 58)
      `there was continuous communication with someone outside who could start emergency procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there was continuous communication between you and someone outside, and emergency procedures could be started from outside (r 65)
      `my employer knew who was inside and got everyone out at the end` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there was a procedure for knowing who was in the space, and everyone was confirmed out when the work ended (rr 66, 67)
      `rescue and first aid procedures were in place and rehearsed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether emergency procedures for rescue and first aid were in place, could be carried out immediately, and had been rehearsed (r 69)
      `I was given information, instruction and training for the space` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were trained in the space's hazards, the controls, protective equipment, the permit and the emergency procedures (r 73)
      `I am an emergency service worker rescuing or giving first aid on my employer's direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an emergency service employee who, at your employer's direction, was rescuing someone from the space or giving first aid in it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer broken the confined space working rules` IS
    `the confined space working rules were contravened (rr 58, 65-67, 69, 73)` `the air was safe or I had air-supplied respiratory equipment` `there was continuous communication with someone outside who could start emergency procedures` `my employer knew who was inside and got everyone out at the end` `rescue and first aid procedures were in place and rehearsed` `I was given information, instruction and training for the space` `I am an emergency service worker rescuing or giving first aid on my employer's direction`

@export Until what day must my employer keep the confined space entry permit for my work (r 64)?
GIVEN `the day the work was completed` IS A DATE @desc The day the work covered by the permit was completed
      `a notifiable incident happened in connection with the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an incident that had to be notified to WorkSafe happened in connection with the work
      `the day of the incident` IS A DATE @desc The day of that incident (any date if there was none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until when must the entry permit be kept` IS
    `the entry permit must be kept until (r 64)` `the day the work was completed` `a notifiable incident happened in connection with the work` `the day of the incident`

§§ `Plant (Part 3.5)`

@export Does Part 3.5 of Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Regulations 2017 (plant) apply to the machine or equipment I work with?
GIVEN `the kind of plant` IS A `Plant kind` @desc The kind of plant: one that cuts, drills, grinds, presses, moulds, mixes, sorts or packages material by mechanical action; one that lifts or moves people or materials; pressure equipment; a tractor; earthmoving machinery; a laser; a scaffold; temporary access equipment; an explosive-powered tool; a turbine; an amusement structure; a ship, boat or aircraft; a road or rail vehicle on a public road or rail; a road or rail vehicle used at a workplace off public roads; or other plant
      `it runs only on manual power or is held up by hand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the plant relies only on manual power or is designed to be supported mainly by hand
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the plant Part apply to this plant` IS
    `Part 3.5 applies to the plant (r 74)` `the kind of plant` `it runs only on manual power or is held up by hand`

@export Is the plant involved in my incident "prescribed plant", so that its collapse, overturning, failure, malfunction or damage must be notified to WorkSafe under s 37(2)(e)(i) of the Act (r 124)?
GIVEN `the kind of plant` IS A `Plant kind` @desc The kind of plant: one that cuts, drills, grinds, presses, moulds, mixes, sorts or packages material by mechanical action; one that lifts or moves people or materials; pressure equipment; a tractor; earthmoving machinery; a laser; a scaffold; temporary access equipment; an explosive-powered tool; a turbine; an amusement structure; a ship, boat or aircraft; a road or rail vehicle on a public road or rail; a road or rail vehicle used at a workplace off public roads; or other plant
      `it runs only on manual power or is held up by hand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the plant relies only on manual power or is designed to be supported mainly by hand
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the plant prescribed plant for incident notification` IS
    `the plant is prescribed for incident notification (r 124)` `the kind of plant` `it runs only on manual power or is held up by hand`

@export Was the guarding on the machine the kind r 99(3) requires (a fixed barrier where no access is needed, an interlocked barrier where it is, and only otherwise a tool-removable barrier or presence-sensing system)?
GIVEN `the guarding used` IS A `Guarding kind` @desc The guarding used: a permanently fixed physical barrier; an interlocked physical barrier; a physical barrier removable only with tools; a presence-sensing safeguarding system (for example light curtains); or no guarding
      `the best guarding that was reasonably practicable` IS A `Guarding kind` @desc The highest kind of guarding that was reasonably practicable (a question for the court, from the same list)
      `access to the guarded area is needed during operation, maintenance or cleaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether people need access to the guarded danger area while the machine is operated, maintained or cleaned
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the guarding the wrong kind` IS
    `r 99(3) was contravened` `the guarding used` `the best guarding that was reasonably practicable` `access to the guarded area is needed during operation, maintenance or cleaning`

§§ `Hazardous substances (Part 4.1)`

@export Must my employer arrange health monitoring for me because of my exposure to a hazardous substance (r 169 and Schedule 9)?
GIVEN `the substance I am exposed to` IS A `Substance` @desc The substance: one of those in Schedule 9 (acrylonitrile, inorganic arsenic, benzene, cadmium, inorganic chromium, creosote, crystalline silica, isocyanates, inorganic mercury, MOCA, organophosphate pesticides, pentachlorophenol, polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons, thallium, vinyl chloride, lead) or another hazardous substance
      `WorkSafe has determined health monitoring is required for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe has determined that health monitoring is required for this substance (answer no if you do not know)
      `my exposure is reasonably likely to harm my health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your exposure, under your conditions of work, is reasonably likely to have an adverse effect on your health
      `my work is a lead process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work is one of the lead processes listed in r 178 (lead smelting, battery work, sanding or burning lead paint, radiator repairs, indoor firing ranges and the like)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer arrange health monitoring for me` IS
    `health monitoring is required (r 169)` `the substance I am exposed to` `WorkSafe has determined health monitoring is required for it` `my exposure is reasonably likely to harm my health` `my work is a lead process`

@export Was I exposed to a hazardous substance above its exposure standard, in breach of r 165?
GIVEN `there is an exposure standard for the substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Safe Work Australia's Workplace Exposure Standards for Airborne Contaminants set a standard for the substance or one of its ingredients
      `the exposure standard` IS A NUMBER @desc The exposure standard, in the units the standard uses (for example mg/m3 or ppm)
      `the concentration I was exposed to` IS A NUMBER @desc The airborne concentration you were exposed to, in the same units as the standard
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I exposed above the exposure standard` IS
    `r 165 was contravened` `there is an exposure standard for the substance` `the exposure standard` `the concentration I was exposed to`

@export Must my employer carry out air monitoring for the hazardous substance I work with (r 166)?
GIVEN `there is an exposure standard for the substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Safe Work Australia's Workplace Exposure Standards for Airborne Contaminants set a standard for the substance or one of its ingredients
      `there are reasonable grounds to be unsure whether the standard is or may be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there are reasonable grounds for uncertainty about whether your exposure is or may be above the standard
      `monitoring is needed to tell whether there is a risk to health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether air monitoring is needed to work out whether there is a risk to health
      `I already have health monitoring that includes biological monitoring for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether r 169 health monitoring that includes biological monitoring (blood, urine or breath tests) is required for this substance
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer carry out air monitoring` IS
    `atmospheric monitoring is required (r 166)` `there is an exposure standard for the substance` `there are reasonable grounds to be unsure whether the standard is or may be exceeded` `monitoring is needed to tell whether there is a risk to health` `I already have health monitoring that includes biological monitoring for it`

@export Until what day must my employer keep my health monitoring report, air monitoring results, lead test results or asbestos medical summary (rr 168, 171, 204, 263, 283, 313: 30 years unless WorkSafe has set a shorter period)?
GIVEN `the day the record was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the report, result or summary was made or received
      `WorkSafe has set a period for this kind of record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe has determined a retention period for this kind of record (answer no if you do not know)
      `the period WorkSafe set, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The period WorkSafe determined, in whole years (any number if none was set)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until when must my health records be kept` IS
    `the record must be kept until` `the day the record was made` `WorkSafe has set a period for this kind of record` `the period WorkSafe set, in years`

§§ `Scheduled carcinogenic substances (Part 4.2)`

@export Is my work with this carcinogen permitted under r 174 (a Schedule 10 prohibited carcinogen only in a licensed laboratory; a Schedule 11 restricted carcinogen only under a licence)?
GIVEN `the carcinogen class` IS A `Carcinogen class` @desc Whether the substance is a Schedule 10 prohibited carcinogenic substance (for example benzidine, 2-naphthylamine), a Schedule 11 restricted carcinogenic substance (for example acrylonitrile, vinyl chloride monomer), or neither
      `my workplace is a laboratory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the workplace is a laboratory
      `I or my employer hold a carcinogens licence for this substance here` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, or the employer you work for, hold a carcinogens licence for this substance at this workplace
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work with this carcinogen permitted` IS
    `the work with the carcinogen is permitted (r 174)` `the carcinogen class` `my workplace is a laboratory` `I or my employer hold a carcinogens licence for this substance here`

@export Must my employer give me a written statement of my work with scheduled carcinogens when I stop working there (r 176)?
GIVEN `the carcinogen class` IS A `Carcinogen class` @desc Whether the substance you worked with is a Schedule 10 prohibited carcinogenic substance, a Schedule 11 restricted carcinogenic substance, or neither
      `I have stopped working at the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ceased to work at the workplace
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be given a statement of my carcinogen work` IS
    `a written statement of carcinogen work is due (r 176)` `the carcinogen class` `I have stopped working at the workplace`

@export Until what day must my employer keep its record of my work with scheduled carcinogens (r 175(3): 30 years from the last day I worked with them)?
GIVEN `the last day I worked with the substance` IS A DATE @desc The last day you worked with a scheduled carcinogenic substance at that employer's workplace
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until when must my carcinogen work record be kept` IS
    `the carcinogen work record must be kept until (r 175(3))` `the last day I worked with the substance`

§§ `Lead (Part 4.3) -- if your work is a lead process`

@export Was the airborne lead at my workplace above the lead exposure standard (r 186: 0.15 mg/m3, and 0.05 mg/m3 from 5 June 2020)?
GIVEN `the day of the measurement` IS A DATE @desc The day the airborne lead was measured
      `the airborne lead in mg per cubic metre` IS A NUMBER @desc The 8-hour time-weighted average concentration of lead dust, mist or fumes in your breathing zone, in milligrams per cubic metre
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the lead exposure standard exceeded` IF
    `the lead exposure standard is exceeded (r 186)` `the day of the measurement` `the airborne lead in mg per cubic metre`

@export Is my work "lead-risk work" under rr 193 and 194 (work in a lead process the employer has identified, or has not been able to rule out, as likely to push blood lead levels over the r 193 figures)?
GIVEN `my work is a lead process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work is one of the lead processes listed in r 178 (lead smelting, battery work, sanding or burning lead paint, radiator repairs, indoor firing ranges and the like)
      `how my employer has classed the process` IS A `Lead identification` @desc How your employer has identified the process under r 194: as reasonably likely to push blood lead levels over the r 193 figures; as not reasonably likely; or not yet either way
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work lead-risk work` IS
    `the work is lead-risk work (rr 193, 194)` `my work is a lead process` `how my employer has classed the process`

@export Did my employer break r 196 (a medical examination and a blood lead test before I first started lead-risk work, and another blood lead test within one month after I started)?
GIVEN `I had a medical examination and a blood lead test before starting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer arranged a medical examination and biological monitoring (a blood lead test) before you first started lead-risk work
      `I had a blood lead test after starting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have had a blood lead test since starting lead-risk work
      `the day I started lead-risk work` IS A DATE @desc The day you started lead-risk work
      `the day of that test` IS A DATE @desc The day of your first blood lead test after starting (any date if there has been none)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did my employer break the lead start-up health checks` IS
    `r 196 was contravened` `I had a medical examination and a blood lead test before starting` `I had a blood lead test after starting` `the day I started lead-risk work` `the day of that test` `today`

@export By what day is my next blood lead test due under r 198?
GIVEN `I am female` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are female
      `I have told my employer in writing I am not of reproductive capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given your employer a written statement that you are not of reproductive capacity (r 179)
      `my last blood lead level in ug per dL` IS A NUMBER @desc Your last blood lead result, in micrograms per decilitre
      `the day of my last blood lead test` IS A DATE @desc The day of your last blood lead test
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By when is my next blood lead test due` IS
    `the next biological monitoring is due by (r 198)`
        (`the employee is treated as a woman of reproductive capacity (r 179)` `I am female` `I have told my employer in writing I am not of reproductive capacity`)
        `my last blood lead level in ug per dL`
        `the day of my last blood lead test`

@export Must my employer take me off lead-risk work immediately (r 199)?
GIVEN `I am female` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are female
      `I have told my employer in writing I am not of reproductive capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given your employer a written statement that you are not of reproductive capacity (r 179)
      `I am pregnant or breastfeeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are pregnant or breastfeeding
      `my blood lead level in ug per dL` IS A NUMBER @desc Your blood lead result, in micrograms per decilitre
      `the day of the result` IS A DATE @desc The day of that blood lead test
      `a doctor says I must be removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a registered medical practitioner, after examining you, is of the opinion that you must be removed from the work
      `controls have failed and my level is likely to reach the removal level` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is an indication that the lead controls have failed so that your blood lead level is likely to reach the removal level
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be taken off lead-risk work` IS
    `the employee must be removed from lead-risk work (r 199)`
        (`the employee is treated as a woman of reproductive capacity (r 179)` `I am female` `I have told my employer in writing I am not of reproductive capacity`)
        `I am pregnant or breastfeeding`
        `my blood lead level in ug per dL`
        `the day of the result`
        `a doctor says I must be removed`
        `controls have failed and my level is likely to reach the removal level`

@export After I was taken off lead-risk work, did my employer provide a medical examination by a doctor within 7 days (r 200(1))? Yes, no, or not yet known while the 7 days are running.
GIVEN `why I was taken off` IS A `Removal ground` @desc Why you were removed: your blood lead level reached the removal level; a doctor's opinion; or failed controls
      `I have had the examination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have had a medical examination by a registered medical practitioner since the removal
      `the day I was taken off` IS A DATE @desc The day you were removed from lead-risk work
      `the day of the examination` IS A DATE @desc The day of that examination (any date if there has been none)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my medical examination after removal in time` IS
    CONSIDER `why I was taken off`
    WHEN `a medical practitioner's opinion (r 199(1)(b))` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF `I have had the examination`
        THEN IF `the day of the examination` `is before` `the day I was taken off`
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `r 200(1) -- medical examination within 7 days after removal` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `provide a medical examination by a registered medical practitioner` (`the number of days from` `the day I was taken off` `to` `the day of the examination`)))
                  WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST TRUE
                  OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF `the number of days from` `the day I was taken off` `to` `today` GREATER THAN 7
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE NOTHING

@export Must my employer keep me off lead-risk work for now (r 201: until my blood lead level is below the return level and a doctor certifies me fit; r 200(2), (3) after a removal for failed controls)?
GIVEN `why I was taken off` IS A `Removal ground` @desc Why you were removed: your blood lead level reached the removal level; a doctor's opinion; or failed controls
      `I am female` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are female
      `I have told my employer in writing I am not of reproductive capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given your employer a written statement that you are not of reproductive capacity (r 179)
      `I am pregnant or breastfeeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are pregnant or breastfeeding
      `my current blood lead level in ug per dL` IS A NUMBER @desc Your latest blood lead result, in micrograms per decilitre
      `the day of the result` IS A DATE @desc The day of that blood lead test
      `a doctor has certified me fit to return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a registered medical practitioner has certified (or, after a removal for failed controls, agreed) that you are fit to return to lead-risk work
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be kept off lead-risk work` IS
    `the employee must be kept off lead-risk work (rr 200, 201)`
        `why I was taken off`
        (`the employee is treated as a woman of reproductive capacity (r 179)` `I am female` `I have told my employer in writing I am not of reproductive capacity`)
        `I am pregnant or breastfeeding`
        `my current blood lead level in ug per dL`
        `the day of the result`
        `a doctor has certified me fit to return`

@export Did my employer tell WorkSafe in writing, within 7 days, that it had identified my work as lead-risk work (r 195(1))? Yes, no, or not yet known while the 7 days are running.
GIVEN `how my employer has classed the process` IS A `Lead identification` @desc How your employer has identified the process under r 194: as reasonably likely to push blood lead levels over the r 193 figures; as not reasonably likely; or not yet either way
      `the day my employer identified it` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer identified the process as reasonably likely to push blood lead levels over the r 193 figures
      `WorkSafe has been notified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has notified WorkSafe in writing of that identification
      `the day WorkSafe was notified` IS A DATE @desc The day of the written notice (any date if there has been none)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was WorkSafe told of the lead-risk work in time` IS
    CONSIDER `how my employer has classed the process`
    WHEN `identified as reasonably likely to exceed the r 193 level` THEN
        IF `WorkSafe has been notified`
        THEN IF `the day WorkSafe was notified` `is before` `the day my employer identified it`
             THEN NOTHING
             ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `r 195(1) -- notice of lead-risk work within 7 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `notify the Authority in writing of the lead-risk work` (`the number of days from` `the day my employer identified it` `to` `the day WorkSafe was notified`)))
                  WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST TRUE
                  OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF `the number of days from` `the day my employer identified it` `to` `today` GREATER THAN 7
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE NOTHING
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Asbestos (Part 4.4) -- if your work exposes you to asbestos`

@export Has my employer breached r 210 (no one exposed above the asbestos exposure standard of 0.1 fibres/ml, and exposure eliminated or else reduced so far as reasonably practicable)?
GIVEN `the asbestos fibre level I was exposed to, in fibres per ml` IS A NUMBER @desc The 8-hour time-weighted average airborne asbestos fibre concentration in your breathing zone, in fibres per millilitre
      `exposure was eliminated or reduced so far as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your exposure to airborne asbestos fibres was eliminated, or else reduced so far as reasonably practicable (a question for the court)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer breached the asbestos exposure duty` IS
    `r 210 was contravened` `the asbestos fibre level I was exposed to, in fibres per ml` `exposure was eliminated or reduced so far as reasonably practicable`

@export Was a broom, brush, high-pressure water jet or power tool used on asbestos in breach of r 216?
GIVEN `such a tool was used on asbestos` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a broom, a brush (other than for sealing), a high pressure water jet, a power tool or a similar tool was used on asbestos
      `the fibre level while it was used, in fibres per ml` IS A NUMBER @desc The airborne asbestos fibre level while the tool was in use, in fibres per millilitre
      `the tool was enclosed or engineering controls kept exposure to half the standard without relying on respirators` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the tool was enclosed or engineering controls were used so that no one was likely to be exposed above half the asbestos exposure standard, without relying on respirators
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was a tool used on asbestos unlawfully` IS
    `r 216 was contravened` `such a tool was used on asbestos` `the fibre level while it was used, in fibres per ml` `the tool was enclosed or engineering controls kept exposure to half the standard without relying on respirators`

@export May I see my employer's asbestos register (r 237: it must be readily accessible to every employee)?
GIVEN `asbestos is present or has been identified at my workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether asbestos is present in a building, structure, ship or plant at your workplace, or has been identified elsewhere there
      `my workplace is a home that is a workplace only because my employer is working there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the workplace is a private home that is a workplace only because your employer was engaged to do work there
      `I am the business's employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed by the business (under a contract of employment or training)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I see my employer's asbestos register` IS
    `the employee may see the employer's asbestos register (r 237)` `asbestos is present or has been identified at my workplace` `my workplace is a home that is a workplace only because my employer is working there` `I am the business's employee`

@export Must I be given asbestos medical examinations (r 262 limited asbestos removal, r 282 licensed asbestos removal, r 311 asbestos-related activities)?
GIVEN `my asbestos work` IS AN `Asbestos work` @desc Your asbestos work: limited asbestos removal work; licensed asbestos removal work (for an asbestos removal licence holder); or asbestos-related activities (handling brake parts, laundering, sampling, enclosing or sealing, hand-drilling and the like)
      `my asbestos work is ongoing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you do the work on an ongoing basis
      `there is a risk of exposure above half the standard, ignoring respirators` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a risk of exposure to airborne asbestos fibres above half the asbestos exposure standard, leaving respirators out of account
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be given asbestos medical examinations` IS
    `asbestos medical examinations are required` `my asbestos work` `my asbestos work is ongoing` `there is a risk of exposure above half the standard, ignoring respirators`

@export Must I have an asbestos medical examination before I start asbestos removal work for this employer or licence holder (r 262(3)(a), r 282(2)(a))?
GIVEN `my asbestos work` IS AN `Asbestos work` @desc Your asbestos work: limited asbestos removal work; licensed asbestos removal work (for an asbestos removal licence holder); or asbestos-related activities (handling brake parts, laundering, sampling, enclosing or sealing, hand-drilling and the like)
      `my asbestos work is ongoing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you do the work on an ongoing basis
      `there is a risk of exposure above half the standard, ignoring respirators` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a risk of exposure to airborne asbestos fibres above half the asbestos exposure standard, leaving respirators out of account
      `I have had an asbestos medical examination before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have had an appropriate asbestos medical examination before
      `the day of my last asbestos medical` IS A DATE @desc The day of your last asbestos medical examination (any date if none)
      `the day I start the work` IS A DATE @desc The day you start the work for this employer or licence holder
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I have an asbestos medical before I start` IS
    `an asbestos examination is required before starting`
        `my asbestos work`
        (`asbestos medical examinations are required` `my asbestos work` `my asbestos work is ongoing` `there is a risk of exposure above half the standard, ignoring respirators`)
        `I have had an asbestos medical examination before`
        `the day of my last asbestos medical`
        `the day I start the work`

@export Must I have an asbestos medical examination after I stop the asbestos work (within 30 days, unless I had one in the preceding year)?
GIVEN `my asbestos work` IS AN `Asbestos work` @desc Your asbestos work: limited asbestos removal work; licensed asbestos removal work (for an asbestos removal licence holder); or asbestos-related activities (handling brake parts, laundering, sampling, enclosing or sealing, hand-drilling and the like)
      `my asbestos work is ongoing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did the work on an ongoing basis
      `there is a risk of exposure above half the standard, ignoring respirators` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there was a risk of exposure to airborne asbestos fibres above half the asbestos exposure standard, leaving respirators out of account
      `I have had an asbestos medical examination before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have had an appropriate asbestos medical examination before
      `the day of my last asbestos medical` IS A DATE @desc The day of your last asbestos medical examination (any date if none)
      `the day I stopped the work` IS A DATE @desc The day you ceased the asbestos work
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I have an asbestos medical after I stop` IS
    `an asbestos examination is required after ceasing`
        (`asbestos medical examinations are required` `my asbestos work` `my asbestos work is ongoing` `there is a risk of exposure above half the standard, ignoring respirators`)
        `I have had an asbestos medical examination before`
        `the day of my last asbestos medical`
        `the day I stopped the work`

@export By what day must my asbestos medical examination after stopping the work be held (within 30 days after I stopped)?
GIVEN `the day I stopped the work` IS A DATE @desc The day you ceased the asbestos work
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when is my asbestos exit medical due` IS
    `the last day for the examination after ceasing` `the day I stopped the work`

@export By what day is my next asbestos medical examination due (intervals of not more than 2 years)?
GIVEN `the day of my last asbestos medical` IS A DATE @desc The day of your last asbestos medical examination
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when is my next asbestos medical due` IS
    `the last day for the next asbestos examination` `the day of my last asbestos medical`

@export Was WorkSafe notified early enough before the asbestos removal work at my workplace began (r 298: at least 24 hours for 10 square metres or less of non-friable material, otherwise at least 5 days)?
GIVEN `the area of asbestos removed, in square metres` IS A NUMBER @desc The total area of asbestos-containing material removed, in square metres
      `the asbestos was friable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the asbestos-containing material was friable (crumbles to powder by hand pressure when dry)
      `hours between the notice and the start of the work` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours before the work began the licence holder notified WorkSafe (0 or less if not notified before the start)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was WorkSafe notified early enough of the asbestos removal` IF
    `hours between the notice and the start of the work` AT LEAST (`the hours of notice required (r 298)` `the area of asbestos removed, in square metres` `the asbestos was friable`)

§§ `Crystalline silica and engineered stone (Part 4.5) -- if your work makes silica dust`

@export Is this product "engineered stone" under r 5 (an artificial product of 1% or more crystalline silica, made by combining natural stone with resins, water or pigments, that hardens)?
GIVEN `its crystalline silica content in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc The crystalline silica content of the product, in per cent by weight
      `it combines natural stone with other materials such as water, resins or pigments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the product is made by combining natural stone materials with other chemical constituents such as water, resins or pigments
      `it hardens` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the product becomes hardened
      `it is an excluded product` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a concrete or cement product, brick, paver or block, ceramic tile, porcelain or sintered stone without resin, roof tile, grout, mortar or render, plasterboard, or a product WorkSafe has determined is not engineered stone
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this product engineered stone` IF
    `the product is engineered stone (r 5)` `its crystalline silica content in per cent` `it combines natural stone with other materials such as water, resins or pigments` `it hardens` `it is an excluded product`

@export Is my work "high risk crystalline silica work" (r 319C: any engineered stone process, or a crystalline silica process likely to exceed half the exposure standard or to risk health; r 319J(4): treated as high risk until shown otherwise)?
GIVEN `my work is an engineered stone process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work is a process involving engineered stone that generates crystalline silica dust (cutting, grinding, polishing and the like)
      `my work is a crystalline silica process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work uses a power tool or mechanical plant on material containing crystalline silica, or is a roadheading, screening, quarrying or tunnelling process involving it, or otherwise exposes you to its dust
      `it is likely to exceed half the exposure standard or to risk health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is reasonably likely to produce respirable crystalline silica above half its exposure standard, or a risk to anyone's health
      `my employer has not been able to tell whether it is high risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has been unable to identify whether the work is high risk crystalline silica work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work high risk crystalline silica work` IF
    `the work is high risk crystalline silica work (rr 319C, 319J(4))` `my work is an engineered stone process` `my work is a crystalline silica process` `it is likely to exceed half the exposure standard or to risk health` `my employer has not been able to tell whether it is high risk`

@export Has my employer breached r 319L (high risk crystalline silica work only with a hazard control statement prepared beforehand and followed)?
GIVEN `my work is an engineered stone process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work is a process involving engineered stone that generates crystalline silica dust (cutting, grinding, polishing and the like)
      `my work is a crystalline silica process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work uses a power tool or mechanical plant on material containing crystalline silica, or is a roadheading, screening, quarrying or tunnelling process involving it, or otherwise exposes you to its dust
      `it is likely to exceed half the exposure standard or to risk health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is reasonably likely to produce respirable crystalline silica above half its exposure standard, or a risk to anyone's health
      `my employer has not been able to tell whether it is high risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has been unable to identify whether the work is high risk crystalline silica work
      `a hazard control statement was prepared before the work began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a crystalline silica hazard control statement (or, for high risk construction work, a safe work method statement covering it) was prepared before the work began
      `the work followed the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work was done in accordance with that statement
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer breached the silica hazard control statement rule` IS
    `r 319L was contravened`
        (`the work is high risk crystalline silica work (rr 319C, 319J(4))` `my work is an engineered stone process` `my work is a crystalline silica process` `it is likely to exceed half the exposure standard or to risk health` `my employer has not been able to tell whether it is high risk`)
        `a hazard control statement was prepared before the work began`
        `the work followed the statement`

@export Has my employer breached the engineered stone controls (r 319S water suppression or on-tool extraction, local exhaust ventilation only if those are not reasonably practicable; r 319V respiratory protective equipment provided and used)?
GIVEN `my work is an engineered stone process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work is a process involving engineered stone that generates crystalline silica dust (cutting, grinding, polishing and the like)
      `I used a power tool or machine on the stone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a power tool or other mechanical plant was used on the engineered stone
      `the dust control used` IS A `Dust control` @desc The dust control used with the tool: an integrated water delivery system; on-tool dust extraction connected to a Class H vacuum or capture system; local exhaust ventilation; or none of these
      `water or on-tool extraction was reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an integrated water system or on-tool extraction was reasonably practicable (a question for the court)
      `I was given respiratory protective equipment and made to use it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer provided you with respiratory protective equipment and ensured you used it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer breached the engineered stone controls` IS
    `rr 319S and 319V were contravened` `my work is an engineered stone process` `I used a power tool or machine on the stone` `the dust control used` `water or on-tool extraction was reasonably practicable` `I was given respiratory protective equipment and made to use it`

@export Is the engineered stone benchtop, panel or slab work I am asked to do prohibited by r 319Y (in force from 1 July 2024)?
GIVEN `the day of the work` IS A DATE @desc The day the work is or was done
      `it is a benchtop, panel or slab` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the engineered stone is a benchtop, panel or slab
      `what I am asked to do` IS AN `Engineered stone activity` @desc What you are asked to do with it: install it; manufacture it; supply it; or process it (cut, grind, polish and the like)
      `the purpose` IS AN `Engineered stone purpose` @desc The purpose: research or analysis; sampling or identifying engineered stone; removing, repairing or modifying engineered stone already installed; disposing of it; or ordinary work
      `the processing follows the engineered stone controls` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any processing is done with the controls of rr 319S-319X (water or on-tool extraction, respiratory protective equipment, training, no compressed-air cleaning)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this engineered stone work prohibited` IS
    `the engineered stone work is prohibited (r 319Y)` `the day of the work` `it is a benchtop, panel or slab` `what I am asked to do` `the purpose` `the processing follows the engineered stone controls`

§§ `Construction (Part 5.1) -- if you do construction work`

@export Is my work "high risk construction work" under rr 321 and 322 (for example a risk of falling more than 2 metres, a trench deeper than 1.5 metres, demolition, asbestos, confined spaces, energised electrical services, moving powered mobile plant)?
GIVEN `my work is connected with building, altering, fitting out, renovating or demolishing a building or structure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work is done in connection with constructing, altering, converting, fitting out, commissioning, renovating, refurbishing, decommissioning or demolishing a building or structure, or the services, excavation or site preparation for it
      `my work is one r 321(3) excludes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is making or assembling fixed plant, prefabrication away from a site set up for the project, routine or minor testing, maintenance or repair, or exploring for or extracting minerals or stone
      `how far a person could fall, in metres` IS A NUMBER @desc The height in metres a person could fall in the work (0 if none)
      `how deep any trench or shaft is, in metres` IS A NUMBER @desc The excavated depth of any trench or shaft in the work, in metres (0 if none)
      `the work has another r 322 feature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is on a telecommunications tower, involves demolition, asbestos, temporary structural support, a confined space, a tunnel, explosives, gas mains, chemical, fuel or refrigerant lines, energised electrical services, a contaminated or flammable atmosphere, tilt-up or precast concrete, roads or railways in use, moving powered mobile plant, artificial extremes of temperature, water with a risk of drowning, or diving
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work high risk construction work` IF
    `the work is high risk construction work (r 322)`
        (`the work is construction work (r 321)` `my work is connected with building, altering, fitting out, renovating or demolishing a building or structure` `my work is one r 321(3) excludes`)
        `how far a person could fall, in metres`
        `how deep any trench or shaft is, in metres`
        `the work has another r 322 feature`

@export Has my employer breached r 327 (high risk construction work that risks anyone's health or safety only with a safe work method statement prepared before it starts, and done in accordance with it)?
GIVEN `my work is connected with building, altering, fitting out, renovating or demolishing a building or structure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work is done in connection with constructing, altering, converting, fitting out, commissioning, renovating, refurbishing, decommissioning or demolishing a building or structure, or the services, excavation or site preparation for it
      `my work is one r 321(3) excludes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is making or assembling fixed plant, prefabrication away from a site set up for the project, routine or minor testing, maintenance or repair, or exploring for or extracting minerals or stone
      `how far a person could fall, in metres` IS A NUMBER @desc The height in metres a person could fall in the work (0 if none)
      `how deep any trench or shaft is, in metres` IS A NUMBER @desc The excavated depth of any trench or shaft in the work, in metres (0 if none)
      `the work has another r 322 feature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is on a telecommunications tower, involves demolition, asbestos, temporary structural support, a confined space, a tunnel, explosives, gas mains, chemical, fuel or refrigerant lines, energised electrical services, a contaminated or flammable atmosphere, tilt-up or precast concrete, roads or railways in use, moving powered mobile plant, artificial extremes of temperature, water with a risk of drowning, or diving
      `the work risks anyone's health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a risk to the health or safety of any person arising from the work
      `a safe work method statement was prepared before the work began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a safe work method statement (or, for asbestos work, an asbestos control plan) was prepared before the work began
      `the work followed the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work was done in accordance with that statement
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer breached the safe work method statement rule` IS
    `r 327 was contravened`
        (`the work is high risk construction work (r 322)` (`the work is construction work (r 321)` `my work is connected with building, altering, fitting out, renovating or demolishing a building or structure` `my work is one r 321(3) excludes`) `how far a person could fall, in metres` `how deep any trench or shaft is, in metres` `the work has another r 322 feature`)
        `the work risks anyone's health or safety`
        `a safe work method statement was prepared before the work began`
        `the work followed the statement`

@export Must my construction project have a principal contractor with a health and safety co-ordination plan (rr 332, 558: projects of $350 000 or more, or $250 000 or more under a contract made before 1 July 2014)?
GIVEN `the cost of the project in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc The cost of the construction project, in dollars, valued as construction work is valued under the Building and Construction Industry Security of Payment Act 2002
      `the day the construction contract was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the construction contract for the project was entered into
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my project have a co-ordination plan` IS
    `the principal contractor's duties apply (rr 332, 558)` `the cost of the project in dollars` `the day the construction contract was made`

@export Is my construction induction card (white card) still current (r 349: it lapses after 2 years without any construction work)?
GIVEN `I hold a construction induction card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a construction induction card
      `the last day I did construction work` IS A DATE @desc The last day you performed construction work
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my construction induction card current` IS
    `the construction induction card is current (r 349)` `I hold a construction induction card` `the last day I did construction work` `today`

@export Is my employer breaking r 341 by letting me do construction work without a current construction induction card (taking the r 342 exemptions into account)?
GIVEN `my employer knowingly lets me do construction work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer knowingly allows you to perform construction work
      `I hold a current construction induction card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current construction induction card
      `it is within my first 28 days in this job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is within 28 days after your employment began
      `I did construction work in the 2 years before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you performed construction work in the preceding 2 years
      `my employer has applied and paid for my induction training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has applied and paid for you to do construction induction training
      `my employer is directly supervising me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is giving you direct supervision, directions, demonstrations and monitoring suited to the work
      `it is within 60 days after I got a construction statement of attainment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is within 60 days after you were issued a construction statement of attainment
      `I hold a pre-1 July 2008 basic induction card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you completed the Construction Industry Basic Induction course before 1 July 2008 and hold the card for it
      `I have recognised evidence of construction induction training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have recognised evidence of general construction induction training (for example an interstate card)
      `that evidence was issued no more than 2 years ago` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that recognised evidence was issued no more than 2 years ago
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer breaking the construction induction card rule` IS
    `r 341 was contravened` `my employer knowingly lets me do construction work` `I hold a current construction induction card` `it is within my first 28 days in this job` `I did construction work in the 2 years before` `my employer has applied and paid for my induction training` `my employer is directly supervising me` `it is within 60 days after I got a construction statement of attainment` `I hold a pre-1 July 2008 basic induction card` `I have recognised evidence of construction induction training` `that evidence was issued no more than 2 years ago`

@export Must WorkSafe be notified before the excavation of this shaft, trench or tunnel at my site begins (rr 354, 355)?
GIVEN `the kind of excavation` IS AN `Excavation kind` @desc The kind of excavation: a shaft; a trench; a tunnel; or another excavation
      `a person could enter it, or it puts someone at risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the excavation will be large or deep enough for a person to enter, or will put anyone's health or safety at risk
      `it is a shaft or trench dug under a building permit in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a shaft or trench dug as part of building work for which a building permit has been issued and is in force
      `it is a mine, bore, quarry, or for emergency work, rescue or burial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the excavation is a mine, a bore under the Water Act 1989, a quarry, or made for emergency work, a rescue or emergency response, or a burial
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must WorkSafe be notified of the excavation` IS
    `WorkSafe must be notified of the excavation (rr 354, 355)` `the kind of excavation` `a person could enter it, or it puts someone at risk` `it is a shaft or trench dug under a building permit in force` `it is a mine, bore, quarry, or for emergency work, rescue or burial`

@export Was WorkSafe notified in writing at least 3 days before the excavation work began (r 355(1))?
GIVEN `the kind of excavation` IS AN `Excavation kind` @desc The kind of excavation: a shaft; a trench; a tunnel; or another excavation
      `a person could enter it, or it puts someone at risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the excavation will be large or deep enough for a person to enter, or will put anyone's health or safety at risk
      `it is a shaft or trench dug under a building permit in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a shaft or trench dug as part of building work for which a building permit has been issued and is in force
      `it is a mine, bore, quarry, or for emergency work, rescue or burial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the excavation is a mine, a bore under the Water Act 1989, a quarry, or made for emergency work, a rescue or emergency response, or a burial
      `WorkSafe was notified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer or self-employed person notified WorkSafe in writing of the intended excavation work
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day of the written notice (any date if there was none)
      `the day the excavation work began` IS A DATE @desc The day the excavation work began
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was WorkSafe notified of the excavation in time` IS
    CONSIDER `Must WorkSafe be notified of the excavation` `the kind of excavation` `a person could enter it, or it puts someone at risk` `it is a shaft or trench dug under a building permit in force` `it is a mine, bore, quarry, or for emergency work, rescue or burial`
    WHEN JUST `required` THEN
        IF NOT `required`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF NOT `WorkSafe was notified`
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE IF `the day the excavation work began` `is before` `the day of the notice`
                  THEN JUST FALSE
                  ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `r 355(1) -- no excavation work until 3 days after the notice` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `commence the construction excavation work` (`the number of days from` `the day of the notice` `to` `the day the excavation work began`)))
                       WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST TRUE
                       OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `Penalties (r 7 and each provision)`

@export What is the most the employer (or other duty-holder) can be fined for breaching this provision of Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Regulations 2017, in penalty units?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision` @desc The provision breached
      `who breached it` IS AN `Offender` @desc Whether the person who breached it is a natural person or a body corporate (a company)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the employer can be fined` IS
    `the maximum fine in penalty units` `the provision` `who breached it`

@export Is a breach of this provision prosecuted as a breach of the Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004 itself (an "Act compliance" provision, r 7), rather than as an offence against the Regulations?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision` @desc The provision breached
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the breach a breach of the Act` IS
    `the provision is enforced through the Act (r 7)` `the provision`
